course: dictionary
lesson: 2531
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Dedication is a good example. «Her dedication to swimming won her the medal» means hard work and loyalty over a long time. Ask: is this about effort, a book, or a church? The words around the word point the way.
explain: Look at «The dedication reads "For my mum"». Here dedication means the words at the start of a book that say who it is for. The clue is reads, and the book-like feel of the sentence. Now test another meaning in the sentence: "The hard work reads 'For my mum'" does not make sense, so that meaning is wrong here.
explain: Other clues come from the topic. «The dedication of a bench to Grandad» is about naming something in honour of someone. «A baby dedication» is a church ceremony where parents promise to bring up their child in the faith. When a word has several meanings, read the whole sentence and check which meaning fits.
fact: Dedication is a noun, and its plural is dedications.
fact: Dedication can mean hard work and loyalty to a task or purpose over a long time.
fact: In books and music, a dedication is the words at the start that say who the work is for.
fact: In church, a dedication is a ceremony that gives a building, or a person, to God or to a holy purpose.
fact: Useful phrases: «dedication to», «with great dedication», and «a dedication service».
exercise: «Her dedication to swimming won her the medal.» What does dedication mean here? | A church ceremony for a new building | A plaque on a bench | A page at the start of a book | *Hard work and loyalty to a task over a long time
exercise: «The dedication reads "For my mum".» Where would you find this dedication? | *At the start of a book | On a sports medal | On the roof of a church | A school dinner menu
exercise: What does «the dedication of a bench to Grandad» mean? | Cleaning a park bench | *Naming something in honour of someone | Hard training for a race | Reading a story aloud
test: «A baby dedication» is most likely which kind of event? | A school trip to the zoo | A cooking lesson | A football match | *A church ceremony where parents promise to bring up their child in the faith
test: Which sentence uses dedication in the church sense? | «Her dedication to swimming won her the medal.» | «The dedication reads "For my mum".» | «The dedication of a bench to Grandad.» | *«The dedication of the new church took place on Sunday.»
exam: Ella reads, «The town held a dedication service for its new hall.» What does dedication most likely mean here? | Hard work over a long time | *A ceremony to give a building to God or to a holy purpose | A plaque with a name on it | Words at the start of a book
